WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.380
The new year is bringing new anime that fans
across the world will love.

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:09.040
Are you ready for a series about historical
warlords in the bodies of modern pet dogs?

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:12.920
How about the story of a girl who realizes
she's the villain in a video game?

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:15.500
All this and more are in store for 2020.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.640
Junji Ito is horror manga's undisputed king.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:24.460
If anything from his vast library of work
can be considered his magnum opus, however,

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:30.420
it is Uzumaki: the slow, sordid chronicle
of one small town's descent into madness.

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:36.920
The story encompasses everything from cannibalistic
body horror to isolation-induced psychosis.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:41.559
Ito's always had a gift for balancing absurdism
with horror, but Uzumaki takes it further

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:42.700
than ever before.

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:48.640
Uzumaki has been adapted before, most notably
as a series of video games and a 2000 live-action

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:49.140
movie.

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:54.040
Nothing, however, has managed to equal its
source material in sheer intensity, until

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:54.540
now.

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:59.920
In partnership with Adult Swim, Production
I.G. has produced a four-episode adaptation

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:03.140
that will air concurrently in Japan and the
United States.

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:08.770
Ito's densely-inked style is a massive challenge
to animate, but teaser trailers reveal uniquely

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:12.740
detailed visuals that should intrigue newbies
and seasoned fans alike.

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:15.060
Just make sure you watch this one with the
lights on.

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:20.960
It might have taken five years longer than
expected, but at last, the finale of the Rebuild

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:23.180
of Evangelion series has a premiere date.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:27.420
These films have always been unique: Though
they're most widely known as a retelling of

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:32.110
the original Neon Genesis Evangelion anime
series, they've grown steadily different from

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:33.840
the source material with each installment.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:38.619
Entirely new characters have taken center
stage, old characters have been woven into

00:01:38.619 --> 00:01:43.020
the narrative far earlier than in the original
series, and a completely different ending

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:44.720
is promised to close out the series.

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:49.490
If the previous films are anything to go by,
3.0+1.0

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:54.079
will be an innovative presentation of everything
that makes Evangelion the anime touchstone

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:59.460
it is, from dazzling animation to a clear-eyed
look at trauma on the precipice of adulthood.

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:04.240
What little has been revealed of the film
promises a breathtaking example of why anime

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:08.760
matters, and why Evangelion won't be fading
into memory any time soon.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:17.380
"It's the duty of the elite to protect the
ignorant masses."

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:23.760
Drifting Dragons follows the experiences of
the crew of a massive "draking" airship dedicated

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:24.920
to hunting dragons.

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:30.000
The anime looks like something of a cross
between Cowboy Bebop and Attack on Titan.

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:35.460
The crew, a ragtag bunch from all walks of
life, live from hunt to hunt, using all their

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:40.350
wits to conquer beasts hundreds of times their
size and ensure full bellies and coffers.

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:45.540
The anime's use of CG promises to retain the
lush detail of the manga while providing its

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:48.500
own spin on Drifting Dragon's cloud-dappled
world.

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:50.800
Early footage is positively sweeping.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:56.200
By air or on land, Drifting Dragons looks
ready to impress with a whole new type of

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:57.200
dragon-slaying.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:03.100
Isekai anime has dominated the scene for years
now with its tales of everyday people dropped

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:04.300
into fantasy worlds.

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:08.800
Sometimes they're reincarnated as low-level
slimes, sometimes they're allowed to bring

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:11.820
their smartphone, and sometimes they're simply
stranded.

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:15.920
One thing unites them all: making escapism
totally literal.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:19.820
My Next Life as a Villainess follows this
formula... for the most part.

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:25.940
Upon sustaining a head injury, our heroine
realizes that she, Duchess Katarina Claes,

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:31.100
was once a high school girl obsessed with
the game Fortune Lover, in which she now resides.

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:36.320
Even more shockingly, she remembers that Katarina
is rival to the player character for the prince's

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:38.720
affections, and thus the bad guy.

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:43.700
Like most isekai, My Next Life is all about
the wonder and strangeness of a different

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:46.740
world, but this one is more obstacle course
than playground.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:51.951
What ensues is a delightfully wry look at
a well-worn genre with as much humor as it

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:52.680
has heart.

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:57.490
Viewers are sure to fall in love with Katarina,
whose dogged determination to survive in a

00:03:57.490 --> 00:04:02.000
world built to destroy her yields fascinating
plot twists and genuine emotion.

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:06.940
Fashion has long proved to be a fertile source
of subject matter for anime.

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:12.550
Samurai Flamenco follows the adventures of
a part-time model, Paradise Kiss takes a look

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:17.200
at the struggling beginnings of a career in
fashion design, and Kill la Kill imagines

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:18.720
clothing as control.

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:23.800
Smile Down the Runway is set to continue the
proud tradition of deeply fashionable anime

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:25.340
with its own DIY flair.

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:30.400
Chiyuki, born into a family already embedded
in the fashion industry, has dreamed of becoming

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:31.600
a model for years.

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:36.780
Unfortunately, adolescence only saw her grow
to 5'2" - far too short to walk the runway

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:38.640
at even the most obscure Fashion Week.

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:44.320
Then she discovers Ikuto, a shy classmate
who has a tremendous talent for fashion design

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:46.380
that he has no idea how to explore.

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:51.080
Together, they decide to take on the world
of fashion despite their handicaps, and manage

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:55.140
to find that what's held them back might actually
be assets in disguise.

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:59.760
Smile Down the Runway's whole-hearted love
of the arts promises to impress - especially

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:04.160
when explored through such dauntless, lovable
characters as Chiyuki and Ikuto.

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:09.900
They might be short, shy, and underfunded,
but as Coco Chanel once said, success is most

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:13.460
often achieved by those who don't know that
failure is inevitable.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:19.380
What a long, strange trip it's been for Masamune
Shirow's landmark science fiction manga.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:24.260
It's been adapted into multiple award-winning
anime series, influenced culture-conquering

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:29.110
art such as The Matrix, been made into a variety
of video games, and most recently, transformed

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:30.770
into a live-action feature.

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:35.820
2020 will see the premiere of yet another
Ghost in the Shell adaptation, this one subtitled

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:42.220
SAC_2045, and it promises to be another take
on the story that's well worth watching.

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:49.280
Uniquely, SAC_2045 will use CGI animation
of a style rarely employed in anime.

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:53.790
The trailer, released by Netflix in October,
reveals a look at the series that is as brief

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:59.090
as it is breathtaking: Major Kusanagi, rendered
in three dimensions, appreciating the quiet

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:00.400
of a desolate landscape.

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:06.100
SAC_2045 looks to be a groundbreaking blend
between an anime standby and new frontiers

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:06.900
in animation.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:11.520
In other words, exactly what a story set on
the bleeding edge of progress should be.

00:06:12.650 --> 00:06:16.389
Keep Your Hands Off Eizouken! consists of
three high school girls looking to make their

00:06:16.389 --> 00:06:17.980
mark on the world of animation.

00:06:18.530 --> 00:06:22.320
These aren't the doe-eyed maidens of K-On!,
however - the members of the Motion Pictures

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:27.080
Club are bona fide weirdos who like army surplus
equipment and obscure animation trivia.

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:32.820
Director Masaaki Yuasa, the visionary behind
Ping Pong and Devilman Crybaby, isn't just

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:37.370
the perfect choice to adapt the oddball manga
- he might just be the only person who could

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:38.660
truly do it justice.

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:42.970
Our heroes inhabit a world that shifts from
the mundane to the magical as they explore

00:06:42.970 --> 00:06:43.960
their imaginations.

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:49.580
That sort of magical realism is precisely
what Yuasa excels at capturing, and likely

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:51.520
what drew him to the manga in the first place.

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:55.860
Like his previous work, Keep Your Hands Off
Eizouken! aims for the heights of what is

00:06:55.860 --> 00:06:59.760
possible in animation, and will likely get
there in high, strange style.

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:05.380
Dorohedoro has been held in high esteem by
manga fans since its 2000 debut.

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:11.780
A post-apocalyptic saga of violence, magic,
and unlikely alliances, its hero is Caiman,

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:16.150
a man stripped of his memories and left with
a reptilian head after a run-in with a sorcerer.

00:07:16.150 --> 00:07:20.980
His world is split in two: There's the Hole,
the derelict home of humanity, and there's

00:07:20.980 --> 00:07:22.160
the world of the sorcerers.

00:07:22.220 --> 00:07:26.440
Those of the latter camp visit the Hole to
practice their abilities on its vulnerable

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:29.700
denizens, Caiman being one of that unfortunate
number.

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:34.760
This cruel dichotomy is disrupted when Caiman
sets out to find the sorcerer who disfigured

00:07:34.770 --> 00:07:39.090
him - and discovers newfound abilities that
will help even the odds between him and those

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:40.560
with magic at their disposal.

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:45.919
Quite a lot of 2000s anime aimed to capture
Dorohedoro's signature blend of horror, humor,

00:07:45.919 --> 00:07:51.050
and fantasy - yet even within that field of
imitators, it has always stood out as singularly

00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:53.340
confident, visionary, and gloriously strange.

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:58.100
Trailers and promotional spots reveal an anime
adaptation every inch as stunning and cheeky

00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:02.670
as its source material, leaving fans with
only one unanswered question: How did it take

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:05.800
this long for Dorohedoro to get an anime of
its own in the first place?

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:12.660
Oda Nobunaga, a feudal lord of 16th-century
Japan, casts a long shadow over the nation's

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:13.160
history.

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:18.720
Regarded as one of Japan's great unifiers,
his reign was as marked by free trade, innovative

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:23.400
art, and advances in military strategy as
it was by brutal suppression of his opponents.

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:28.720
Unsurprisingly, his fictional portrayals number
in the hundreds: Nobunaga has appeared in

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:32.680
everything from Pokemon to the Sengoku Basara
video games.

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:36.340
Sometimes he's the villain, sometimes he's
the hero, and sometimes he's somewhere in

00:08:36.340 --> 00:08:41.240
between, but over and over again, he is used
as an inspiration for storytelling.

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:46.320
Despite all this competition, Oda Cinnamon
Nobunaga will still manage to provide a new

00:08:46.320 --> 00:08:50.140
twist on the tale... by portraying the legendary
lord as a dog.

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:55.630
In this anime, Nobunaga's death in the infamous
Honno-ji Incident was immediately followed

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:59.200
by his reincarnation as a modern-day shiba
inu named Cinnamon.

00:08:59.480 --> 00:09:04.620
But Nobunaga isn't alone - it turns out that
a plethora of figures from Japan's Sengoku,

00:09:04.620 --> 00:09:08.880
or "warring states" period, have been brought
back to life as pet dogs.

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:12.880
Legendary tactician Date Masamune is now a
French bulldog.

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:17.020
Fearsome commander Takeda Shingen is now a
Pomeranian.

00:09:17.180 --> 00:09:20.920
Whether you're a longtime Japanese history
buff or a curious fan looking for something

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:25.839
new, Oda Shinamon Nobunaga looks to be an
anime unlike anything else on the air.

00:09:26.839 --> 00:09:31.410
It's not every anime series that can release
a single piece of key visual art and inspire

00:09:31.410 --> 00:09:36.080
ardent discussion, but anything made by Studio
Trigger tends to get that treatment.

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:41.500
Since its 2013 debut with Little Witch Academia,
Trigger has produced smash hit after smash

00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:42.000
hit.

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:48.120
Its most recent work, the psychedelic action
fantasia Promare, managed to make $1 million

00:09:48.130 --> 00:09:52.670
on only 30 screens in North America, prompting
a return to theaters that few anime films

00:09:52.670 --> 00:09:55.470
have ever been granted in the English-speaking
market.

00:09:55.470 --> 00:09:57.100
Enter Brand New Animal.

00:09:57.100 --> 00:10:02.220
All fans have to slaver over is a single image:
what looks to be an anthropomorphic wolf in

00:10:02.230 --> 00:10:06.290
a trench coat and a basketball-toting girl
with squirrel-like features, standing against

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:10.170
a neon-splashed backdrop of skyscrapers and
billboards.

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:14.649
If the upright cheetah in athleisure behind
them is any indication, theirs is a world

00:10:14.649 --> 00:10:19.740
of humanoid animals like Zootopia or Beastars,
albeit one rendered according to Trigger's

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:22.460
highly saturated, ultra-modern aesthetic.

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:27.020
So far, those are the only details fans have
to pick apart - but Trigger has inspired the

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:31.640
confidence to make even those scant clues
enough to make Brand New Animal an anime to

00:10:31.640 --> 00:10:32.140
watch.

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:36.640
There are series that take a while to find
their footing, and then there is anime like

00:10:36.640 --> 00:10:37.760
The Promised Neverland.

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:43.540
Season 1 wastes no time stranding its fans
alongside its heroes in a truly disorienting

00:10:43.540 --> 00:10:48.500
premise: a world ruled by demons, in which
oblivious children are raised as meat.

00:10:48.860 --> 00:10:53.440
Emma, Ray, and Norman, whose lives have been
lived entirely within the confines of the

00:10:53.441 --> 00:10:58.589
sun-dappled orphanage that is, in fact, a
farm, stumble upon this horrifying fact by

00:10:58.589 --> 00:10:59.200
accident.

00:10:59.580 --> 00:11:04.399
The first season sees their daring quest to
escape take shape and ultimately succeed,

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:08.680
climaxing in their first sunrise beyond the
walls of the orphanage in the season finale.

00:11:08.940 --> 00:11:13.570
It was an immediate sensation, hooking fans
left and right with its potent blend of horror

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:16.510
and heart, all brought home by a kid's-eye
view.

00:11:16.510 --> 00:11:20.480
The second season promises more of this, at
an even more startling level of intensity:

00:11:20.720 --> 00:11:24.940
Though the kids have escaped their captors,
they have become completely alone.

00:11:25.440 --> 00:11:29.860
What does the world beyond the walls even
look like, if demons who eat children command

00:11:29.860 --> 00:11:31.420
such power within it?

00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:34.240
Who of their number will survive it, and how?

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:39.640
What structures of power maintain the orphanage
system, and what will it take to rend it asunder?

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:44.510
Some of these questions might be answered
in season 2, some might not, but we'll all

00:11:44.510 --> 00:11:45.580
be watching to find out.

00:11:46.840 --> 00:11:49.180
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:11:49.420 --> 00:11:52.840
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
movies are coming soon.

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:56.680
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

